# KH environment. Copy to .env at the target repo root and fill in.
#
# THIS BUILD RUNS CLAUDE CODE AS THE CODING AGENT (coding_agent: claude_code).
# Authentication is Claude Code's own: either an interactive login already on
# this machine, or ANTHROPIC_API_KEY set here (or a Bedrock/Vertex setup —
# whatever `claude` itself is configured with).
#
# `model:` entries are claude aliases (opus | sonnet | haiku) or full model ids.
# A `provider/` prefix is allowed and stripped (`anthropic/opus` -> `opus`), so
# rosters written in the provider/id habit keep working.
#
# Nothing validates the credential for you. `agents.validate()` checks that the
# claude CLI is on PATH and the model string is non-empty, not that the account
# is reachable — an auth failure shows up when that agent runs, not at startup.

ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# Optional overrides
# CLAUDE_CODE_PATH=claude          # claude binary if not on PATH
# KH_CC_CONTEXT_WINDOW=200000    # context ceiling for the UI's context bar
# ENGINEER_NAME=                   # engineer lane label, defaults to git user.name

# Optional existing non-superuser credential for execution.infrastructure.worker_env.
# Add its name to defaults.env_allowlist when supplied through .env.
# Explicit ${KH_WORKER_DATABASE_URL} references fail before planning if empty.
# KH_WORKER_DATABASE_URL=
